# LTNT.APP — environment configuration (copy to .env; ALL keys are OPTIONAL)
#
# The core app — Generate, latent Explore/Cluster, the GLASS make-more loop,
# and the persistent Board — runs with NO keys at all (local models on your GPU).
# The keys below ONLY enable the optional external EDIT backends. Leave them
# unset to run fully locally; the edit providers that lack a key are simply
# unavailable (the server returns a clear "…_API_KEY is not configured" message).
#
# NEVER commit your filled-in .env. (.env is gitignored; this .example is the template.)

# --- Optional image-EDIT backends (each independent) ---
REVE_API_KEY=         # Reve image edit (the default "EDIT WITH: REVE" provider)
OPENAI_API_KEY=       # OpenAI image edit/generate provider
GEMINI_API_KEY=       # Google AI Studio key for the NanoBanana (Gemini image) edit provider

# --- Local model resolution (self-hosting) ---
# The generation backends (FLUX.1-dev / SANA / Krea-2-Raw) load from your HF cache.
# On a normal machine HF_HOME is enough; on clusters with flaky offline resolution,
# stage the snapshot locally and point an explicit *_LOCAL_PATH at it.
# HF_HOME=~/.cache/huggingface
# FLUX_LOCAL_PATH=/path/to/models--black-forest-labs--FLUX.1-dev/snapshots/<rev>
# KREA_LOCAL_PATH=/path/to/krea2/snapshot
